<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="biscuit-hazel" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Biscuits (Grandma Hazel)</title>

  <p>
    Ingredients
  </p>
  <tabular>
    <row>
      <cell>2 cups flour</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 tablespoon baking powder</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 teaspoon salt</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
    <cell><m>\frac{1}{4}</m> cup shortening</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{2}{3}</m> to <m>\frac{3}{4}</m> cup milk or buttermilk</cell>
    </row>
  </tabular>

  <p>Instructions
    <ol>
      <li>
        <p>
          Combine flour, baking powder, and salt.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Cut in shortening until mixture resembles coarse crumbs.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          With a fork, blend in just enough milk until dough leaves the sides of the bowl.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Knead gently 2 to 3 times on a lightly floured surface.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Roll dough to <m>\frac{1}{2}</m>-inch thickness, and cut biscuits without twisting the biscuit cutter.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Spray baking sheet with cooking spray, and place biscuits on the baking sheets, 1 inch apart for crisp-sided biscuits or almost touching for softer sided biscuits.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Bake at <m>500^\circ</m> for 8 to 10 minutes.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </p>

  <p>
    Notes:
    <ul>
      <li>
        <p>
          
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </p>
</section>